# Byte-for-byte fidelity, everywhere.
#
# update.js verifies each downloaded file against a SHA-256 in version.json.
# Those hashes are computed from the working tree, and the download comes from
# raw.githubusercontent.com, which serves the blob exactly as stored. If git
# rewrote line endings on checkout, a Windows clone would hash CRLF files
# against LF blobs and every update would fail the integrity check.
#
# So: no newline conversion for anything, ever.
* -text

*.ico binary
*.png binary
